@startuml sequence-transfer-between-currencies
title Transfer between wallets of different currencies
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Client\n(via individuals-api)" as Client
participant "transaction-service" as TS
participant "currency-rate-service" as CRS
database "transaction DB\n(shard of the user)" as DB

note over Client
  individuals-api checks the client's token, adds X-User-Uid,
  calls transaction-service with its service token and passes every answer back as is
end note
note across
  Validation, wallet checks, offer token checks, repeats and DB errors: see transaction-service sequence-transfer.
  Every call to currency-rate-service carries the incoming service token of individuals-api, passed on as is;
  circuit breaker (circuit-breaker); 404 → 422 RATE_NOT_FOUND; timeout, 5xx, open breaker →
  503 RATE_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE; 400, 401, 403 → 500 INTERNAL_ERROR, the answer only in the log.
end note

== init: nothing is written ==
Client -> TS: POST transfer/init (UAH wallet → EUR wallet, amount 150.00)
TS -> DB: both wallets of the user
alt same currency
    TS -> TS: sequence-transfer, no rate
else different currencies
    opt source currency is not USD
        TS -> CRS: GET /api/v1/rates?from=UAH&to=USD
        CRS --> TS: 200 rate 0.024
        TS -> TS: amount in USD = 150.00 × 0.024 = 3.60 (2 digits, HALF_UP)
    end
    alt amount in USD < transfer.min-conversion-amount-usd (1.00, application.yml)
        TS --> Client: 400 AMOUNT_TOO_SMALL
    else enough
        TS -> CRS: GET /api/v1/rates?from=UAH&to=EUR\n(not called when the target is USD: the rate above is used)
        CRS --> TS: 200 rate 0.0221
        TS -> TS: fee 0.5% = 0.75, total 150.75 UAH;\ntargetAmount = 150.00 × 0.0221 = 3.32 EUR\n(full rate, only the result rounded: 2 digits, HALF_UP)
        alt targetAmount = 0.00
            TS --> Client: 400 AMOUNT_TOO_SMALL
        else balance < total
            TS --> Client: 400 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS
        else enough
            TS -> TS: offerToken signs the terms with rate and targetAmount, 5 minutes
            TS --> Client: 200 amount, fee, total, rate, targetAmount, expiresAt, offerToken
        end
    end
end

== confirm: one DB transaction, the rate comes from the token, currency-rate-service is not called ==
Client -> TS: POST transfer/confirm (offerToken)
TS -> TS: token checks, claim of requestId, expiry
group one DB transaction
    TS -> DB: lock both wallets
    TS -> DB: UPDATE source balance − 150.75 UAH
    TS -> DB: UPDATE target balance + 3.32 EUR (targetAmount from the token)
    TS -> DB: UPDATE transactions SET status = 'COMPLETED', rate = 0.0221, target_amount = 3.32
    TS -> DB: COMMIT
end
TS --> Client: 200 COMPLETED, transactionId
@enduml
